        "event": "Flood Watch",
        "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
        "senderName": "NWS Baltimore MD/Washington DC",
        "headline": "Flood Watch issued August 2 at 10:37AM EDT until August 3 at 2:00AM EDT by NWS Baltimore MD/Washington DC",
        "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of western Maryland, including the following\nareas, Central and Eastern Allegany, Eastern Garrett, Extreme\nWestern Allegany and Western Garrett, western Virginia, including\nthe following areas, Eastern Highland and Western Highland, and\neastern West Virginia, including the following areas, Eastern\nGrant, Eastern Mineral, Eastern Pendleton, Hampshire, Hardy,\nWestern Grant, Western Mineral and Western Pendleton.\n\n* WHEN...Through late tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nLow-water crossings may be flooded.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Multiple rounds of heavy showers and thunderstorms are\nforecast to move across the area beginning this morning, and\ncontinuing through this evening. Many areas could see 1 to 2\ninches of rain. Areas that see multiple rounds of heavy rain\ncould receive localized amounts of 3 to 4 inches.\n- Please visit www.weather.gov/safety/flood for flood safety\nand preparedness information",
        "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
        "response": "Prepare",
        "note": null,
